# Performance Optimization

## Background Data Preloading
The app implements comprehensive background preloading to eliminate loading delays:

### Preloading Strategy
- **Silent Execution**: Starts immediately when homepage loads
- **Parallel Fetching**: All data fetched concurrently
- **Memory Caching**: Data stored in Zustand store
- **Fallback Mechanism**: Individual API calls if preloading fails

### Implementation
```typescript
// In HomePage.tsx
useEffect(() => {
  // Start preloading immediately
  dataPreloader.preloadAllData();
}, []);
```

## React Query Optimization

### Cache Configuration
```typescript
// Optimized cache settings
{
  staleTime: 1000 * 60 * 60, // 1 hour
  gcTime: 1000 * 60 * 60 * 24, // 24 hours
  enabled: !!layoutId // Conditional fetching
}
```

### Preloaded Data Priority
```typescript
// Hooks use preloaded data when available
queryFn: async () => {
  const preloadedData = dataPreloader.getPreloadedData();
  if (preloadedData) {
    return preloadedData.layouts; // Instant access
  }
  return apiService.getLayouts(); // Fallback
}
```

## Component Optimization

### React.memo Usage
```typescript
// Memoize expensive components
const DynamicSvgDiagram = React.memo(({ 
  layoutName, 
  layoutImage,
  manualFields, 
  measurements,
  autoCalculatedFields 
}) => {
  // Component logic
});
```

### useCallback for Event Handlers
```typescript
const handleMeasurementChange = useCallback((fieldName: string, value: number) => {
  // Handler logic
}, [currentShape.measurements, autoCalculationRules, currentShapeIndex]);
```

### useMemo for Expensive Calculations
```typescript
const calculatedFields = useMemo(() => {
  return applyAutoCalculationRules(measurements, rules);
}, [measurements, rules]);
```

## State Management Optimization

### Selective Updates
```typescript
// Only update if values actually changed
const hasChanges = Object.keys(measurements).some(
  key => currentShape.measurements[key] !== measurements[key]
);

if (!hasChanges) return state; // Skip update
```

### Immutable Updates
```typescript
// Always create new objects
const newShapes = [...state.selectedShapes];
newShapes[shapeIndex] = {
  ...currentShape,
  measurements: { ...currentShape.measurements, ...measurements }
};
```

## Image Optimization

### SVG Preloading
```typescript
// Preload SVG images to prevent layout shifts
const svgPromises = layouts.map(async (layout) => {
  if (layout.layout_image) {
    await fetch(layout.layout_image);
  }
});
```

### Next.js Image Component
```typescript
import Image from 'next/image';

<Image
  src={cutout.image}
  alt={cutout.name}
  width={64}
  height={64}
  className="object-cover w-full h-full"
  onError={(e) => {
    const target = e.target as HTMLImageElement;
    target.src = '/assets/images/fallback.jpg';
  }}
/>
```

## Bundle Optimization

### Dynamic Imports
```typescript
// Lazy load heavy components
const HeavyComponent = dynamic(() => import('./HeavyComponent'), {
  loading: () => <div>Loading...</div>
});
```

### Tree Shaking
- Use named exports for better tree shaking
- Avoid importing entire libraries
- Use specific imports from large packages

## Network Optimization

### Parallel API Calls
```typescript
// Fetch multiple resources in parallel
const [fields, rules, groups] = await Promise.all([
  apiService.getLayoutFields(layoutId),
  apiService.getAutoCalculationRules(layoutId),
  apiService.getLayoutFieldGroups(layoutId)
]);
```

### Request Deduplication
- React Query automatically deduplicates requests
- Same queries within 1000ms are batched
- Reduces unnecessary network requests

## Memory Management

### Cleanup Functions
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  
  return () => {
    controller.abort(); // Cancel pending requests
  };
}, []);
```

### Event Listener Cleanup
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  const handleResize = () => { /* logic */ };
  window.addEventListener('resize', handleResize);
  
  return () => {
    window.removeEventListener('resize', handleResize);
  };
}, []);
```

## Monitoring and Metrics

### Performance Monitoring
```typescript
// Track loading times
console.time('data-preload');
await dataPreloader.preloadAllData();
console.timeEnd('data-preload');
```

### Error Tracking
```typescript
// Track performance issues
try {
  await expensiveOperation();
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Performance issue:', error);
  // Report to monitoring service
}
```

## Best Practices Summary
- **Preload Critical Data**: Background preloading eliminates delays
- **Optimize Re-renders**: Use React.memo, useCallback, useMemo
- **Efficient State Updates**: Only update when necessary
- **Image Optimization**: Preload SVGs, use Next.js Image
- **Bundle Splitting**: Lazy load heavy components
- **Network Efficiency**: Parallel requests, request deduplication
- **Memory Cleanup**: Proper cleanup in useEffect
- **Monitor Performance**: Track metrics and errors
